# CSA Alpha-3 Canon Audit Report

## Executive Summary
✅ Canon Layer P0-P4 Established: FAN Registry active, ASI defined, Hookpoints declared
🎯 CSA Objective: All new artifacts must check FAN Registry before implementation

## Audit Findings

### 1. FAN Registry - ACTIVE ✅
- 6/6 FANs registered: gguf-verify, tokenizer, kv-cache, first-token, inference-runtime
- Clear owners/stewards assigned
- Assembly graph: tokenizer → gguf_loader → kv_cache → inference_engine → sampler

### 2. Hookpoints - DECLARED ✅
- gguf-loader.ail: owner=hacedle (immutable), input=gguf_path, output=model_metadata+tensor_index
- Restrictions: no_duplicate_parser, no_local_metadata_reimplementation

### 3. ASI Integration - DEFINED ✅
- gguf-loader.ail: requires reuse of hacedle::x::loader::gguf::{loader_std, header, tensor_index}
- Prohibits: brain/master/provider/gguf/{metadata.rs, tensor.rs}
- Output: hookpoint brain.gguf.loader

### 4. Authority Boundary - ESTABLISHED ✅
- ownership.ail: hacedle owns x/loader/gguf/*, x/provider/candle/*
- brain/master owns src/provider/gguf/loader.rs (DELEGATES_ONLY), src/tokenizer/
- brain/master steward_of: brain.gguf.loader

### 5. CSA Audit Scripts - READY ✅
- 5 independent scripts owned by CSA: gguf_verify.py, tokenizer_roundtrip.py, first_token.py, inference_chain.py, kv_cache_validation.py

### 6. Code Implementation - IN PROGRESS ⚠️
- brain/master/src/provider/gguf/loader.rs: Now delegates to hacedle::GgufLoader
- ISSUE: Still hardcodes architecture: "qwen2" (should read from metadata)
- FIXED: Removed hardcoded tensor_count/vocab_size/context_length

